{
  "version": 11,
  "randomSeed": "60aaabb3b222eafd5980b8ae82ddf990",
  "expressions": {
    "list": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "72",
        "text": "The identity below is true for all x, where a and b are constants. Find the value of ab. Choices: A is 12, B is 24, C is 6, D is 18."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "90",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "\\left(ax+4\\right)\\left(3x^{2}-bx+5\\right)=18x^{3}-6x^{2}+18x+20"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "77",
        "text": "First, find a by matching the leading terms on each side."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "91",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "a=\\frac{18}{3}"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "79",
        "text": "Substitute that value of a into the identity."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "92",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "\\left(6x+4\\right)\\left(3x^{2}-bx+5\\right)=18x^{3}-6x^{2}+18x+20"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "84",
        "text": "A regression on the identity lets Desmos find b. Regressing both constants at once gives ambiguous results, so a is solved first."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "73",
        "color": "#2d70b3",
        "latex": "\\left(6x_{1}+4\\right)\\left(3x_{1}^{2}-bx_{1}+5\\right)\\sim18x_{1}^{3}-6x_{1}^{2}+18x_{1}+20",
        "residualVariable": "e_{1}",
        "regressionParameters": {
          "x_{1}": 1,
          "b": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "87",
        "text": "The two constants multiply to the value below."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "93",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "6\\cdot3"
      }
    ]
  }
}
